//? Title: PCG32: actual XSH-RR operands
//? Subtitle: Canonical C++ producers, original fixtures and explicit controls
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
The old64-bit state supplies the xorshift and rotation; the LCG simultaneously
advances modulo2^64 with an odd increment. Each native next_u64 call
concatenates two consecutive32-bit outputs, first in the high half. The
selectable increment has only63 effective selector bits: selectors differing in
bit63 alias. Distinct increments are not a guarantee of statistical
independence. This simulation generator is not a cryptographic primitive.
[The author reference|https://www.pcg-random.org/download.html] supplies
the32-bit construction. No dataset is needed.
)

\toc

> Mechanism and scope

The old64-bit state supplies the xorshift and rotation; the LCG simultaneously
advances modulo2^64 with an odd increment. Each native next_u64 call
concatenates two consecutive32-bit outputs, first in the high half. The
selectable increment has only63 effective selector bits: selectors differing in
bit63 alias. Distinct increments are not a guarantee of statistical
independence. This simulation generator is not a cryptographic primitive.
[The author reference|https://www.pcg-random.org/download.html] supplies
the32-bit construction. No dataset is needed.

$$ s_{n+1}=6364136223846793005s_n+c\pmod{2^{64}},\qquad c=2\,\mathrm{sequence}+1\pmod{2^{64}}. $$

> A tiny actual producing history

The table and native diagram use the same producing run. Captured records own
their values; the report does not reconstruct the algorithm.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/pcg32_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
    dm::random::Pcg32 rng(42, 54);
    auto t = rng.next_u32_trace();
    std::print("| before | after | xorshifted | rotation | output |\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: " "|\n| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n",
               t.before, t.after, t.xorshifted, t.rotation, t.output);
    dm::graphics::Diagram d;
    d.node("n0", {0, 0}, std::format("Actual old state\n{}", t.before));
    d.node("n1", {8, 0},
           std::format("Actual XSH then rotate\n{} / {}", t.xorshifted,
                       t.rotation));
    d.node("n2", {16, 0}, std::format("Actual 32-bit output\n{}", t.output));
    d.edge("n0", "n1").edge("n1", "n2");
    d.save_svg("build/pcg32_tiny.svg");
}
```
